---
title: Payment: what if the response is lost
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant P as Payment worker
  participant G as Gateway
  participant C as Customer
  participant H as Payment webhook
  participant R as Payment reconciler
  participant O as Orchestrator
  P->>P: attempt PENDING (committed first)
  P->>G: POST /v1/orders (receipt = order id)
  alt Case A: create-order reply lost
    G--xP: order created, reply lost (timeout)
    Note over P: attempt UNKNOWN, NO second call
    R->>G: look up the order by receipt
    G-->>R: order found
    Note over R: attempt AWAITING_PAYMENT
  else reply received
    G-->>P: order id, AWAITING_PAYMENT
  end
  C->>G: pays, money is taken
  alt Case B1: webhook arrives
    G->>H: payment.captured (signed)
    Note over H: verify, store in inbox, answer 200, worker applies
  else Case B2: webhook lost or service down
    G--xH: webhook not received (gateway retries)
    R->>G: poll the order (about every 15 s)
    G-->>R: payment captured
  end
  Note over P,R: decide with OUR clock: before the deadline SUCCEEDED, after it FAILED plus refund
  P-->>O: reply Succeeded or Failed (outbox)
